---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Contact ContextLife"
  description="Get in touch with ContextLife — corrections, source suggestions, partnership questions, or feedback on the assessment."
  path="/contact"
  eyebrow="Contact"
  heading="Get in touch."
  lede="We read everything, and we especially want to hear about errors. Accuracy is the whole point of this site."
>
  <h2>Email us</h2>
  <p>
    The best way to reach us is by email at
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We aim to respond within a
    few business days.
  </p>

  <h2>What to write about</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Corrections.</strong> If a figure looks wrong or out of date, tell us
      — include the page and, if you can, a source. We will review and fix or
      annotate it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Source suggestions.</strong> If there is a study or dataset we should
      be citing, send it along.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Feedback.</strong> Did the assessment or an insight page help you see
      something more clearly — or get something wrong about your situation? That
      feedback shapes what we build.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Press &amp; partnerships.</strong> For media or collaboration
      enquiries, use the same address with "Press" in the subject line.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we cannot do</h2>
  <p>
    We cannot offer personal financial, medical, legal, or psychological advice,
    and we cannot respond to crises. If you are struggling or in danger, please
    contact a qualified professional or your local emergency or crisis service. In
    the U.S., you can call or text <strong>988</strong> to reach the Suicide and
    Crisis Lifeline. Outside the U.S., search for your local crisis line.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Anything you email us is used only to respond to you. We do not add you to
    marketing lists. See our <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> and
    <a href="/how-we-use-data">how we use data</a> for the full picture.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
